      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-325423",
      ":question/problem": "A university surveyed $750$ students who were selected at random from its campus and asked, \u201cDo you plan to attend the spring sports festival this year?\u201d Of those surveyed, $62%$ responded \u201cno.\u201d\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all students at the university, exactly $62%$ do not plan to attend the spring sports festival this year.\n2. If another $750$ students selected at random from the university were surveyed, the proportion who say \u201cno\u201d is likely to be close to $62%$.\n3. If $750$ students selected at random from a different university were surveyed, the proportion who say \u201cno\u201d is likely to be close to $62%$."
    },
