      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-325424",
      ":question/problem": "A health department surveyed $1,000$ residents who were selected at random from a small city and asked, \u201cHave you received a flu vaccine in the past year?\u201d Of those surveyed, $40%$ responded \u201cyes\u201d.\n\nBased on this result, which of the following conclusions are appropriate?\n\n1. Of all residents in the city, approximately $40%$ have received a flu vaccine in the past year.\n2. If another $1,000$ residents selected at random from the city were surveyed, the proportion who say \u201cyes\u201d is likely to be close to $40%$.\n3. If $1,000$ residents selected at random from a different city were surveyed, the proportion who say \u201cyes\u201d is likely to be close to $40%$."
    }
